  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">DCM DenizBank GB</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Stakeholder effects: IFC anticipates that the proposed investment will contribute to increased access to climate finance in T&#xfc;rkiye. It is expected that 100 percent of the proceeds of the investment will be used to finance green finance projects with considerable GHG emission savings potential.
Market creation: The investment is expected to strengthen the adoption of climate finance in T&#xfc;rkiye. IFC anticipates that the proposed Green Bond issuance by the Bank will further promote the growth of sustainable bonds in the Turkish market through demonstration and replication channels.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The proposed investment entails IFCs subscription to a Green Bond of up to US$100 million to be issued by DenizBank A.S. (DenizBank or the Bank), with the total bond issuance size expected to be up to US$275 million. DenizBank will use the bond proceeds to expand its green finance-eligible loan portfolio, specifically targeting corporate and commercial borrowers as well as small and medium enterprises (SMEs).</narrative>
  </description>
